19000  This is where you set solutions for your puzzles. You can program moveable parts so that they must be in a specific location for the game to recognize the puzzle's solution.\n\nYou can also program parts that may be altered in "physical state." For example, you can program the balloon so that the puzzle will not be solved until the balloon has been popped.\n\nYou can only have eight individual solutions in any puzzle. All the solutions you program must occur or remain true at the same time, or the game won't recognize the solution.
